[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: MIL-STD-498 IRS (Interface Requirements Specification) - ADAS Control Module

[SECTION]
TITLE: 1. Scope

[SECTION]
TITLE: 1.1 Identification

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IRS-001
TITLE: Interface Requirements Identification
STATEMENT: This document shall be identified as the Interface Requirements Specification (IRS) for the Advanced Driver Assistance System (ADAS) Control Module, version 1.0, following MIL-STD-498 and automotive interface standards.
RATIONALE: Proper interface requirements identification ensures configuration management and interface traceability for automotive safety systems.

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: 1.2 System overview

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IRS-002
TITLE: Interface Overview
STATEMENT: The ADAS Control Module shall provide comprehensive interface requirements for sensor integration, vehicle control, human machine interface, and external communication for automotive safety-critical applications.
RATIONALE: Interface overview establishes the foundation for all interface requirements in the automotive safety domain.

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: 1.3 Document overview

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IRS-003
TITLE: Interface Document Structure
STATEMENT: This document shall be organized into sections covering interface identification, interface requirements, interface standards, and interface validation following MIL-STD-498 and automotive interface standards.
RATIONALE: Structured organization facilitates interface requirements review and validation for safety-critical systems.

[/SECTION]

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: 2. Referenced documents

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IRS-004
TITLE: Interface Standards
STATEMENT: The interface requirements shall comply with AUTOSAR interface standards, CAN bus protocols, Ethernet automotive standards, and automotive cybersecurity standards for interface implementation.
RATIONALE: Compliance with established automotive interface standards ensures system compatibility and safety.

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: 3. Interface requirements

[SECTION]
TITLE: 3.1 Sensor interface requirements

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IRS-005
TITLE: Radar Sensor Interface
STATEMENT: The system shall interface with front, rear, and side radar sensors using CAN bus protocol with data rates up to 1Mbps, supporting object detection, distance measurement, and velocity calculation.
RATIONALE: Radar sensor interfaces are critical for accurate environmental perception and safety system operation.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IRS-006
TITLE: Camera Sensor Interface
STATEMENT: The system shall interface with front and rear cameras using Ethernet protocol with data rates up to 100Mbps, supporting image processing, lane detection, and traffic sign recognition.
RATIONALE: Camera sensor interfaces are critical for visual perception and safety system operation.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IRS-007
TITLE: Ultrasonic Sensor Interface
STATEMENT: The system shall interface with ultrasonic sensors using CAN bus protocol for short-range object detection and parking assistance with data rates up to 500kbps.
RATIONALE: Ultrasonic sensor interfaces support parking assistance and low-speed safety features.

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: 3.2 Vehicle control interface requirements

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IRS-008
TITLE: Brake Control Interface
STATEMENT: The system shall interface with brake control unit using secure CAN bus protocol with redundant communication paths, supporting emergency braking and adaptive cruise control functions.
RATIONALE: Brake control interfaces enable critical safety functions and accident prevention.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IRS-009
TITLE: Engine Control Interface
STATEMENT: The system shall interface with engine control unit using CAN bus protocol for adaptive cruise control and speed management with appropriate safety interlocks.
RATIONALE: Engine control interfaces enable adaptive cruise control and speed management functions.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IRS-010
TITLE: Steering Control Interface
STATEMENT: The system shall interface with steering control unit using secure CAN bus protocol for lane keeping assistance and emergency steering with safety validation.
RATIONALE: Steering control interfaces enable lane keeping assistance and emergency steering functions.

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: 3.3 Human machine interface requirements

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IRS-011
TITLE: Instrument Cluster Interface
STATEMENT: The system shall interface with instrument cluster using CAN bus protocol for displaying ADAS status, warnings, and system information with priority-based messaging.
RATIONALE: Instrument cluster interfaces ensure driver awareness and system transparency.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IRS-012
TITLE: Head-Up Display Interface
STATEMENT: The system shall interface with head-up display using Ethernet protocol for displaying critical warnings and traffic sign information with low latency requirements.
RATIONALE: Head-up display interfaces enhance driver awareness and safety information display.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IRS-013
TITLE: Center Console Interface
STATEMENT: The system shall interface with center console using Ethernet protocol for system configuration, user preferences, and detailed system information display.
RATIONALE: Center console interfaces enable system configuration and user preference management.

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: 3.4 External communication interface requirements

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IRS-014
TITLE: Over-the-Air Update Interface
STATEMENT: The system shall provide secure over-the-air update interface using encrypted communication protocols for software updates and configuration management.
RATIONALE: Over-the-air update interfaces enable remote software updates and system maintenance.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IRS-015
TITLE: Diagnostic Interface
STATEMENT: The system shall provide diagnostic interface using standard automotive diagnostic protocols for system troubleshooting and maintenance support.
RATIONALE: Diagnostic interfaces enable system troubleshooting and maintenance support.

[/SECTION]

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: 4. Interface standards

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IRS-016
TITLE: Communication Protocols
STATEMENT: The system shall support CAN bus, Ethernet, and FlexRay communication protocols with appropriate data rates, error detection, and redundancy for automotive applications.
RATIONALE: Standard communication protocols ensure system compatibility and reliability.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IRS-017
TITLE: Data Formats
STATEMENT: The system shall use standardized data formats including AUTOSAR message formats, sensor data formats, and diagnostic data formats for interface compatibility.
RATIONALE: Standardized data formats ensure interface compatibility and system integration.

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: 5. Interface validation

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IRS-018
TITLE: Interface Testing
STATEMENT: The system shall undergo comprehensive interface testing including protocol validation, data format validation, and performance testing for all interfaces.
RATIONALE: Comprehensive interface testing ensures interface reliability and system compatibility.

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: 6. Notes

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IRS-019
TITLE: Interface Guidelines
STATEMENT: The interface requirements shall follow automotive interface guidelines, safety standards, and industry best practices for interface design and implementation.
RATIONALE: Interface guidelines provide guidance for interface design and ensure safety compliance.

[/SECTION] 